{"repositoryId":1276657831,"availability":"available","full":"MSKazemi/yazses","name":"yazses","description":"Free, open-source, fully-offline-by-default voice dictation for Linux (X11 & Wayland), macOS & Windows. Hold a key, speak, release — on-device faster-whisper types it into any app. Also transcribes recordings & captures meetings with speaker labels. No cloud, no account, no subscription.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":29,"forks":36,"created":"2026-06-22T07:15:03Z","updated":"2026-10-15T13:56:35Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mskazemi.com/yazses/","topics":["accessibility","assistive-technology","dictation","faster-whisper","linux","macos","meeting-notes","meeting-transcription","offline","privacy","speaker-diarization","speech-recognition","speech-to-text","transcription","voice-commands","voice-dictation","voice-typing","wayland","whisper","windows"],"demo":"https://mskazemi.com/yazses/try-without-installing.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.158Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.158Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.158Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.158Z","stars":29,"forks":36}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Hold a key, speak, and your words are typed into any app. Nothing leaves your computer by default.","More than a dictation box — it also takes voice commands, transcribes recordings you already have, and can capture a whole meeting with speaker labels. Everything runs offline on your own CPU. Dictation works out of the box; the extras beyond it are opt-in and off by default.","Hold the key and just talk — by default everything you say is typed at the cursor. YazSes also recognises a set of voice commands (a fast regex grammar; a 0.5B SLM router for phrasings the grammar misses is designed but not wired yet) that map to editor/terminal key sequences instead of being typed:"],"features":["Fully offline — no audio, no text, nothing leaves the machine by default; no cloud, API key, or subscription","Hold-to-talk dictation — type into any focused app on Linux, macOS, or Windows","Meeting Mode — hands-free whole-meeting capture → speaker-labelled transcript, plus optional local-LLM minutes (summary, decisions, action items); audio is deleted after transcription unless you keep it","Offline file transcription — yazses transcribe turns any audio/video into txt/md/srt/vtt/json, with optional who-said-what speaker tags","Voice commands — editor/terminal actions (undo, save, go-to-line, run tests, rename…) via regex grammar + an optional SLM router"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a18b7ca6e77d2a58bfefc816a9d8b4da3f19680fda71b3583c232fec80fe4bd1","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.303Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.303Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Hold a key, speak, and your words are typed into any app. Nothing leaves your computer by default.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"There is no network call at any step, no account, and no API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Use it when audio must not be sent to Google, Apple, Microsoft, or Otter — because the meeting is confidential, the machine is air-gapped, or you simply don't want a subscription.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"yazses setup ends by printing a numbered finish-installing checklist of the steps only you can do — the input-group re-login, calibrate your voice (yazses mic-level --set), and yazses start — and offers to run the mic calibration for you right away.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Yes — YazSes runs natively on Linux (X11 and Wayland), transcribes locally on the CPU, and needs no cloud service or API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a18b7ca6e77d2a58bfefc816a9d8b4da3f19680fda71b3583c232fec80fe4bd1","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.304Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T13:56:35Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:16.306Z","hash":"a18b7ca6e77d2a58bfefc816a9d8b4da3f19680fda71b3583c232fec80fe4bd1","originalBytes":63641,"storedBytes":63641,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["yazses","docs","voice","install","index.md","what","dictation","run","offline","key","linux","text","commands","optional","windows","macos","model","audio","command","editor","meeting","start","hold","nothing","one","see","want","app","daemon","free","python","runs","tests","cloud","cpu","hold-to-talk","input","microphone","need","only","pipx","terminal","bash","first","on-device","open","own","set","there","does","grammar","injection","minutes","transcription","already","any","build","capture","config","doctor","each","every","faster-whisper","hotkey","how","right","setup","slm","speaker","step","wayland","without","accessibility","after","apt","cli","everything","file","line","local","needs","source","speak","speech","undo","add","built","default","features","full","installs","latest","man","mode","new","opt-in","out","over","published","rather","reference","release","research","snap","talon","tools","typed","words","works","comparison","corpus","fully","group","guide","installing","just","list","machine","mic","page","plus","quick","read","regex","router","running","rust","status","system","test","threshold","types","upgrade","vad","version","when","window","work","x11","actually","ag